[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-4555"] :question/problem "For $x>2$, find ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)={\\int }_{2}^{\\sqrt{x}}\\frac{1}{2-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute ${f}^{′}(x),$ we first make the substitution $u=\\sqrt{x}$ and then we apply the chain rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{\\int }_{2}^{\\sqrt{x}}\\frac{1}{2-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{2}^{u}\\frac{1}{2-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe integrand is continuous on $[2,u],$ and so by FTC II we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2-{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2-{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2-(\\sqrt{x})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}(2-x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-75220/selection/25e79e727255861283911302d786395ec011d653dabd38ff2a3be06bef4a2bb0" :answer/id #uuid "910d7a2d-690e-54d1-8815-c962dfda7f44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{g}^{′}(5)=-51" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75220/selection/f92a96b1b57845738d8bd0993974b7246cc519ee14f28ce30e375caf513aa8ea" :answer/id #uuid "1611b5c7-2808-5940-8ef1-0071982d690e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{g}^{′}(5)=-49" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75220/selection/5315f3ecb025ddf65847b596c8e9168908ca8e26f103daf382b7fd8c44876b7b" :answer/id #uuid "fa77798b-86c7-50f7-9460-8b847644bcea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{g}^{′}(5)=43" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75220/selection/db2b572813166a658d982c4c7a04f88a1f680d3405adf67a04683ad03b39d6dd" :answer/id #uuid "3bfbc517-7955-5a72-be04-6f8116b76b8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{g}^{′}(5)=39" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75220/selection/dc565660d43d10b78c43b221c704470deb10c5df57fa346b888112f549d57895" :answer/id #uuid "6da3aa3e-1a39-5e03-a56c-9ccc60bd4012" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{g}^{′}(5)=50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75220/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "59b24bc6-6bec-5d87-a059-3b98d93075da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75220/selection/25e79e727255861283911302d786395ec011d653dabd38ff2a3be06bef4a2bb0" :answer-field/choices ["q-75220/selection/25e79e727255861283911302d786395ec011d653dabd38ff2a3be06bef4a2bb0" "q-75220/selection/f92a96b1b57845738d8bd0993974b7246cc519ee14f28ce30e375caf513aa8ea" "q-75220/selection/5315f3ecb025ddf65847b596c8e9168908ca8e26f103daf382b7fd8c44876b7b" "q-75220/selection/db2b572813166a658d982c4c7a04f88a1f680d3405adf67a04683ad03b39d6dd" "q-75220/selection/dc565660d43d10b78c43b221c704470deb10c5df57fa346b888112f549d57895"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75220" :question/id #uuid "04689b09-69a7-501a-b2fc-c0ba3b87804e" :question/math-academy-id "q-75220" :question/problem "Let $f(x)={x}^{2}+5x+1.$ Find ${g}^{′}(5)$ given the function is defined by $g(x)={\\int }_{x}^{7}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "In this example, the variable limit $x$ is located on the lower limit. To apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit. Using the properties of definite integrals, we can write\n\n$$\ng(x)={\\int }_{x}^{7}({t}^{2}+5t+1)\\,\\text{d}t=-{\\int }_{7}^{x}({t}^{2}+5t+1)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by FTC II, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{\\int }_{x}^{7}({t}^{2}+5t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{\\int }_{7}^{x}({t}^{2}+5t+1)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{7}^{x}({t}^{2}+5t+1)\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+5x+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of ${g}^{′}(5),$ we substitute $x=5$ in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(5) & =-({5}^{2}+5\\cdot 5+1) \\\\  & =-(25+25+1) \\\\  & =-51\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-75220/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5075a64-0f91-58cf-b01b-5b71035f0680"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75220"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117291/selection/0d474ca756c76f6ecddcd5fcfb411f0292ef0ce725af778ee27af0d5dc8595bc" :answer/id #uuid "8e9a46e6-fbd7-5405-9402-e9fc0047ccf1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117291/selection/ae5f5a98d3d858b97b34fa2158dce643243be52513bbacae3b36e31617d78718" :answer/id #uuid "723b769e-a6bd-53f1-bd52-58f138ebd19c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3-4{e}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117291/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "ac6f4488-6cc5-538f-a565-b8ac6cffef44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117291/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "39ea09d4-69b3-5406-8754-367858191628" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117291/selection/7fa94b3b79db00bdba0b669b402267da59d8cf40da5a2f37e7aa76c6ed1f2576" :answer/id #uuid "dc5f80ec-3a43-5624-bc0b-43e47a7494b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2+5e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117291/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6eecd04d-b3de-5834-bf4c-562fcb4318f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117291/selection/0d474ca756c76f6ecddcd5fcfb411f0292ef0ce725af778ee27af0d5dc8595bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-117291/selection/0d474ca756c76f6ecddcd5fcfb411f0292ef0ce725af778ee27af0d5dc8595bc" "q-117291/selection/ae5f5a98d3d858b97b34fa2158dce643243be52513bbacae3b36e31617d78718" "q-117291/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-117291/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-117291/selection/7fa94b3b79db00bdba0b669b402267da59d8cf40da5a2f37e7aa76c6ed1f2576"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117291" :question/id #uuid "5345f4d0-20b2-5008-8103-b715a5705623" :question/math-academy-id "q-117291" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(0)$ if $f(x)={\\int }_{x}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, both the lower and upper limits contain a variable. However, to apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit only. So, we can split the integral into two integrals, and rewrite them so that in both cases the variable is on the upper limit. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{x}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{x}^{a}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{a}^{x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is any constant number between $x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\nThe integrand ${e}^{1-{t}^{2}}$ is continuous for all $t,$ so applying the FTC II gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{\\int }_{a}^{x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-{e}^{1-{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({\\int }_{a}^{u}{e}^{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-{e}^{1-{x}^{2}}+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x){e}^{1-{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =-{e}^{1-{x}^{2}}-{e}^{1-{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =-{e}^{1-{x}^{2}}-{e}^{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\nFinally, we can compute ${f}^{′}(0).$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0) & =-{e}^{1-{0}^{2}}-{e}^{{sin}^{2}⁡0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & =-{e}^{1-0}-0 \\\\  & =-e.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-117291/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a0f285ec-4f37-5d0d-a65c-be3ca48c740f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117291"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117292/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "108d0a5a-a0fc-593b-9c3f-43c46566491e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117292/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "08383a5e-262e-5ecf-a09a-8ac9d8a98df8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117292/selection/c20b3bddb7df6db04d3c2b36fc9e5a84a64bfcdd3a76e711949f68dceef7ff48" :answer/id #uuid "04d22ae3-2fba-515f-8199-72512c411d1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt[3]{1-e}+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117292/selection/677f6febefd166aff9825811fb4c560318daf239822af96c60097bfe308c5125" :answer/id #uuid "12c0e594-5c1d-559b-849f-55cab6bd1351" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt[3]{1-e}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117292/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "35d734a7-fa06-598e-bc02-367c8cda50a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117292/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f7fba06-d2fb-5a65-b4a9-dbf68dcbd802" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117292/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-117292/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-117292/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-117292/selection/c20b3bddb7df6db04d3c2b36fc9e5a84a64bfcdd3a76e711949f68dceef7ff48" "q-117292/selection/677f6febefd166aff9825811fb4c560318daf239822af96c60097bfe308c5125" "q-117292/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117292" :question/id #uuid "47a1e353-0abf-5596-bc63-479c1e9efffa" :question/math-academy-id "q-117292" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(0)$ if $f(x)={\\int }_{-{e}^{2x}}^{x}\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, both the lower and upper limits contain a variable. However, to apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit only. So, we can split the integral into two integrals, and rewrite them so that in both cases the variable is on the upper limit. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-{e}^{2x}}^{x}\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{-{e}^{2x}}^{a}\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{x}\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{a}^{-{e}^{2x}}\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{x}\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is any constant number between $-{e}^{2x}$ and $x.$\n\nThe integrand $\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}+1}$ is continuous for all $t,$ so applying the FTC II gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{\\int }_{a}^{-{e}^{2x}}\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{a}^{x}\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{-{e}^{2x}}\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}t)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\int }_{a}^{x}\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({\\int }_{a}^{u}\\sqrt[3]{{t}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}t)+\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{3}+1} \\\\  & =-(-2{e}^{2x})\\sqrt[3]{{u}^{3}+1}+\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{3}+1} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2x}\\sqrt[3]{(-{e}^{2x})^{3}+1}+\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{3}+1} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2x}\\sqrt[3]{1-{e}^{6x}}+\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{3}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the substitution $u=-{e}^{2x}.$\n\nFinally, we can compute ${f}^{′}(0).$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0) & =2{e}^{2(0)}\\sqrt[3]{1-{e}^{6(0)}}+\\sqrt[3]{{0}^{3}+1} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt[3]{1-1}+\\sqrt[3]{1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-117292/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a0f285ec-4f37-5d0d-a65c-be3ca48c740f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117292"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-333583/field-1/03984ced119046cd5d84212495ac425aee3ef638a7b33680251b19b8fe8894bc" :answer/id #uuid "b6c9710b-2cc6-58b2-887f-9f935486e343" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-e^x\\sin(e^{2x})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-333583/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "83489642-2ffa-5db2-a79f-78b742327bab" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-333583/field-1/03984ced119046cd5d84212495ac425aee3ef638a7b33680251b19b8fe8894bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-333583/field-1/03984ced119046cd5d84212495ac425aee3ef638a7b33680251b19b8fe8894bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-333583" :question/id #uuid "d4b317c5-e5ec-5e4f-8ea0-05929d43147f" :question/math-academy-id "q-333583" :question/problem "Find ${g}^{′}(x)$ for $g(x)={\\int }_{{e}^{x}}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t.$\n\n${g}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To compute ${g}^{′}(x),$ we first make the substitution $u={e}^{x}$ and then we apply the chain rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{\\int }_{{e}^{x}}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{u}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe limit $u$ is located on the lower limit. To apply FTC II, we need the variable to be on the upper limit. Using the properties of definite integrals, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{u}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(-{\\int }_{3}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{3}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by FTC II, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{u}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{3}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(({e}^{x})^{2})) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{2x})) \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{2x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-333583/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0703e1b-2b81-5b95-b2ad-a7e42e702c21"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-333583"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
